;;; Create, query, change, validate, and write YAML data
;;;
;;; This code showcases the API provided by library `(lispkit yaml)`. It builds a
;;; small "configuration toolkit" around a deployment manifest. The manifest is a
;;; YAML stream with two documents. It uses anchors, aliases, and merge keys. The
;;; code parses the manifest, queries it via YAML references, converts it to Scheme
;;; data, reports problems with their source positions, changes the manifest
;;; destructively and non-destructively, writes it back with different formatting
;;; options, converts it to JSON, collects statistics with the streaming parser, and
;;; finally reads YAML 1.1 style booleans with a custom schema.
